1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,800
Two feet wide, zero visibility.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,840
An American rescue man feels his way through a flooded cave passage,

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:10,300
passing a sedated child hand -to -hand in the pitch dark.

4
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:15,040
His name has never been in a single movie made about this rescue.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,780
Neither has the second Thai Navy diver who died because of this mission,

6
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:23,200
or the federal jury trial a billionaire's tweet actually produced.

7
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:27,280
This is the real story of the Tham Luang Cave Rescue,

8
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:30,020
not the one you already watched in a theater or on Netflix.

9
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,660
12 boys and their coach went into a cave in Northern Thailand.

10
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:40,200
All 13 came out alive. Almost nothing else about that sentence is as simple as it sounds.

11
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,840
You're watching Mind Wide.

12
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:49,360
This is the full real story of the 2018 Tham Luang Cave Rescue.

13
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,520
What actually happened inside the cave,

14
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:53,080
the American rescue team,

15
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:55,380
every film left out, the federal trial,

16
00:00:55,620 --> 00:00:56,940
a billionaire's tweet produced,

17
00:00:56,940 --> 00:01:01,800
and the real 2026 echo that shows this story isn't finished yet.

18
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:07,100
Chapter one, the cave. June 23rd,

19
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:09,860
2018, Chiang Rai, Northern Thailand.

20
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,640
12 boys from the Wild Boars Youth Football Club,

21
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:17,520
ages 11 to 16, walk into Tham Luang Cave with their assistant coach after practice.

22
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:20,760
Coach Ekapol Shantawong is 25.

23
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:22,620
He was orphaned as a child,

24
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:25,020
spent years as a novice Buddhist monk,

25
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:26,600
and is legally stateless,

26
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:28,980
along with at least three of the boys on this team.

27
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:34,060
Unseasonal monsoon rain floods the cave's lower passages while they're inside,

28
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:36,360
cutting off the exit and pushing the group deeper.

29
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:38,280
That evening, the head coach,

30
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,080
a different man named Noperat,

31
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:42,360
finds 20 missed calls from parents.

32
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:49,000
Thai Navy SEAL divers reach a chamber called Pattaya Beach two days later and turn back.

33
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:51,400
The water beyond it has never been mapped.

34
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,580
Cave diving is not scuba diving.

35
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:57,300
In zero visibility, in a current,

36
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:00,020
a diver has to feel the walls with both hands,

37
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:01,760
laying a guideline as they go,

38
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:05,780
because turning around and simply swimming back is not always possible.

39
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:08,700
That is why this call went out,

40
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,120
not to the Thai military alone,

41
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:15,560
but to a small, specific community of civilian cave diving experts scattered across

42
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,600
Britain, Australia, Belgium,

43
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:23,180
and beyond. June 29th, Thailand's prime minister visits the site in

44
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:26,940
person and asks publicly that the country stay focused on the rescue,

45
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:29,940
not on blaming a coach for taking children into a cave.

46
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:34,660
Chapter two, 13 days and a country's worth of water.

47
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:39,480
Within a week, the operation scales past 600 people,

48
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:42,060
then past 10 ,000 engineers,

49
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:45,540
soldiers, and volunteers from 17 countries.

50
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:52,480
Over 100 farmers watch roughly 5 ,500 acres of their own rice fields deliberately flooded,

51
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:55,860
diverted on purpose to slow water pouring into the mountain.

52
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,120
It is barely mentioned in any film made about this rescue.

53
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,840
More than one billion literates of water are pumped out of the mountain,

54
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:06,260
roughly 400 Olympic swimming pools,

55
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:11,080
while engineers drill over 100 boreholes from the surface hunting for a shaft that never

56
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:15,880
finds them. Officials debate teaching the boys to dive out themselves.

57
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:21,080
Rejected, they are untrained children in a technical cave system that has already turned

58
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:26,240
back Navy seals. Waiting out the roughly four -month monsoon season with

59
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:28,620
food ferried in was the safest plan on paper.

60
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:31,720
It was rejected too, dwindling oxygen,

61
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:36,180
rising water, and 13 people who could not simply wait that long.

62
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:42,600
By July 4th, pumps are removing water at a peak rate of 1 .6 million literates

63
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:47,220
an hour. Engineers will end up drilling past 100 boreholes into the mountain,

64
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,280
searching for a shaft that never once finds the group.

65
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:54,240
Chapter three, the Americans nobody put in the movie.

66
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:59,420
June 28th, a team from the 353rd Special Operations Group,

67
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:02,240
U .S. Air Force, lands in Chiang Rai from Okinawa,

68
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,660
Japan. Two of their pararescuemen,

69
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:08,240
tech sergeants Jamie Brisbane and John Merchant,

70
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,740
are stationed inside a two -foot -wide,

71
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:13,920
zero -visibility flooded passage called Sump Three,

72
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:16,420
moving the boys hand -to -hand between chambers.

73
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:21,260
Neither of the two big films about this rescue mentions them by name.

74
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:25,580
This is not the same as saying the divers you've heard of didn't matter.

75
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:30,800
It means the full team was bigger and more international than either screen version had

76
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:33,880
room for. The technique itself,

77
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:38,660
moving a person hand -to -hand through a passage too narrow to swim through side -by

78
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:42,440
-side was later demonstrated using a training dummy at a U .S.

79
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:44,760
base in Japan for exactly this reason.

80
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:47,300
The real thing happened in total darkness,

81
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:49,560
with no camera able to survive the trip.

82
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:54,600
British divers Jason Mallinson and Chris Jewell joined the extraction team as well,

83
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,220
alongside Volanthin and Stanton.

84
00:04:56,920 --> 00:05:02,020
By the final count, 13 international cave divers and five Thai Navy SEALs made up

85
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:05,000
the extraction team. Chapter four,

86
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:08,760
found. July 2nd, evening,

87
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:12,960
nine days in. British divers John Volanthin and Rick Stanton,

88
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:16,340
laying line two and a half kilometers into the flooded system,

89
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:19,760
surface at a mud slope and find all 13 of them alive.

90
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,000
The exchange caught on tape.

91
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:26,120
How many of you? 13, 13, brilliant!

92
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,560
Nine days with almost no food,

93
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:32,220
all 13 conscious, coherent,

94
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:35,420
and alive. It is to this day,

95
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:39,520
one of the only rescues of its kind in recorded history to end this way.

96
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:44,340
Two freelance divers, Ben Remenetz and Mux Impala Jhaka,

97
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:46,360
reportedly reached the group first,

98
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:48,880
ahead of the British team every retelling credits.

99
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:52,840
It would take three years before Volanthin and Stanton acknowledged them publicly.

100
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:57,160
Australian anesthetist Richard Harris and his diving partner,

101
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:58,880
veterinarian Craig Challen,

102
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:01,540
are flown in specifically for what comes next.

103
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:05,760
Harris will end up making the single riskiest call of the entire operation.

104
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:09,620
Chapter five, The Billionaire's Submarine.

105
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:15,900
July 8th, Elon Musk tweets that a child -sized submersible built from a spare Falcon

106
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:18,120
9 rocket part is on its way to help.

107
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:22,420
Two days later, the rescue is completed without it.

108
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,440
The operation's on -site commander,

109
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:28,980
Narongsack Osatnakorn, calls the device impractical for the cave's narrow,

110
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:32,720
twisting passages. The device itself,

111
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:35,380
nicknamed Wild Boar after the trapped team,

112
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:40,540
was built by SpaceX and boring company engineers out of a spare Falcon 9 rocket part

113
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,280
and actually flown to the site.

114
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,760
On July 13th, British caver,

115
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:49,440
Vernon Unsworth, who had lived locally and helped coordinate the rescue,

116
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:53,800
tells CNN the submarine was a PR stunt and that Musk should,

117
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,740
in his words, stick his submarine where it hurts.

118
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:00,900
Two days after that, Musk fires back on Twitter.

119
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:04,140
Sorry, pedo guy, you really did ask for it.

120
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:06,880
He deletes it and apologizes within days.

121
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:11,100
Chapter six, the trial nobody filmed.

122
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:14,700
Unsworth sues for defamation that September,

123
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:19,460
seeking $190 million. In private emails to a reporter,

124
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:23,920
Musk goes further, calling Unsworth a child rapist with no evidence.

125
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:30,200
Musk goes further still in a private email exchange with a reporter calling Unsworth

126
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,200
a child rapist and claiming,

127
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:36,280
with no evidence at all, that he had moved to Thailand for a child bride.

128
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:40,460
The reporter had not agreed to keep any of it off the record.

129
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,520
He published the emails in full.

130
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:46,220
A judge rules Unsworth a private citizen,

131
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:48,280
not a public figure, for these statements,

132
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,980
meaning Musk would only need to have acted carelessly,

133
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,800
not maliciously, to lose.

134
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:56,580
That single ruling matters more than it sounds.

135
00:07:57,020 --> 00:08:01,620
A public figure has to prove a defendant knew a statement was false or recklessly ignored

136
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:05,640
the truth. A private citizen only has to prove ordinary carelessness.

137
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:08,880
The bar for Unsworth to win had just gotten lower.

138
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:14,560
December 3rd, 2019, a four -day jury trial in Los Angeles.

139
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:19,680
Musk testifies. He apologizes to Unsworth on the stand and says no one actually understood

140
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,160
the tweet to mean pedophile.

141
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,580
Musk's defense laid out at trial.

142
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,360
That Piddo guy was old South African slang for a creepy old man,

143
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,920
not a literal accusation.

144
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:33,000
And that the tweet, which never actually named Unsworth,

145
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:36,120
couldn't reasonably be read as being about him specifically.

146
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:41,220
Unsworth's team sought $190 million in damages,

147
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:45,080
pointing to Musk's roughly $20 billion net worth at the time.

148
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:49,880
The judge instructed the jury the private emails could describe Musk's state of mind,

149
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,920
but could not, on their own,

150
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:56,320
prove defamation. The jury deliberates for under an hour.

151
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,180
They find Musk not liable.

152
00:08:58,180 --> 00:09:01,240
Zero damages. A civil verdict,

153
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:05,620
not a criminal one. By one juror's own account afterward,

154
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:09,080
the panel never even reached the question of whether the accusation was true.

155
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:13,820
They simply weren't convinced a reasonable person could tell an unnamed tweet was about

156
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:16,740
Unsworth at all. Chapter seven,

157
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:19,500
the extraction nobody could have filmed.

158
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,020
Oxygen inside the boys' chamber falls toward 15%,

159
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:28,160
well below breathable. Officials abandon every plan except one,

160
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:31,640
sedate all 13, and carry them out through the flooded cave,

161
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:36,460
one at a time. Every other option had already failed or been rejected.

162
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:39,200
This was the last plan left on the table,

163
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:42,780
and nobody involved was certain it would work on a single child,

164
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:46,900
let alone all 13. The Real Drug Protocol,

165
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:50,860
published later in the New England Journal of Medicine by the operation's own medical

166
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:53,160
team, an anti -anxiety tablet,

167
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:55,540
atropine, then a ketamine injection,

168
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:58,820
chosen specifically because it doesn't suppress breathing.

169
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:04,220
Ketamine specifically, because unlike almost every other sedative available,

170
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:06,800
it doesn't suppress the drive to keep breathing,

171
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:11,800
something that mattered enormously for a swim that would last hours through cold water.

172
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:17,100
Each boy is fitted with a full -face oxygen mask and physically carried through the flooded

173
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:18,560
passages by a lead diver,

174
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:23,980
sedated the entire way. The order they came out in wasn't decided by the doctors.

175
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:25,960
The boys decided it themselves,

176
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:28,200
days earlier, trapped in the dark.

177
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:31,020
Whoever lived farthest from the cave should go first,

178
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:33,000
so they wouldn't have as far to bike home.

179
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:38,520
July 6th, Thai Navy SEAL volunteer Saman Kunan runs out of his own air,

180
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:41,400
returning from delivering oxygen tanks and dyes.

181
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,940
He is posthumously promoted seven ranks by royal command.

182
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:48,540
18 months later, a second SEAL,

183
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:53,660
Petty Officer Beirut Pakbara dies from a blood infection contracted during the same

184
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:57,240
mission. Almost no retelling of this story mentions his name at all.

185
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:01,280
Two deaths on two completely different timelines,

186
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:03,740
both caused by the same 18 -day mission.

187
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:06,320
Most retellings only remember one of them.

188
00:11:07,660 --> 00:11:13,360
July 10th, 18 divers, 13 from around the world and five Thai Navy SEALs

189
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,820
bring out the last four boys,

190
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:17,960
their coach and the medical team who never left their side.

191
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,040
18 days after they walked in,

192
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:24,020
everyone is out. By the third and final day,

193
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:29,240
what had taken roughly three hours per boy on day one had been cut to just over two.

194
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:33,400
The team had gotten faster with every single life they carried out.

195
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:37,080
Chapter eight, What the Story Left Out.

196
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:42,700
Freelance divers Ben Remenetz and Maksim Poljaka reportedly located the group first.

197
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:47,140
The British divers' every film credits didn't publicly acknowledge them for three years.

198
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,620
Not because their contribution was invented,

199
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:55,480
because the two men every screen adaptation lionizes hadn't been the ones to find them

200
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:58,400
first. And that fact took years to become public.

201
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:04,960
Within weeks, Thailand fast -tracked citizenship for Ekapol and the stateless boys on

202
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:09,880
the team, members of the Thai -Lu ethnic minority who had lived in Thailand their whole

203
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:12,520
lives without ever legally belonging to it.

204
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:16,660
Ekapol and the boys had lived their entire lives in Thailand,

205
00:12:16,660 --> 00:12:19,100
gone to Thai schools, spoken Thai,

206
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:22,040
without ever holding the legal right to a Thai passport,

207
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,340
a bank account, or in some cases,

208
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:26,880
even to travel outside their home district.

209
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,560
Within days of the rescue,

210
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:33,820
studios and streamers were racing to buy the rights to tell these boys stories.

211
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:39,020
Netflix's exclusive deal is the specific reason the Oscar -nominated documentary team

212
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:40,560
never got to speak with them at all.

213
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:45,900
That auction is why the boys never appear at all in the Oscar -nominated documentary

214
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:50,560
about their own rescue, and why the scripted Netflix series exists specifically because

215
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,260
it, not the documentary team,

216
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:54,620
held the rights to tell their side of it.

217
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:57,940
The documentary that did get real access,

218
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:00,100
built from 87 hours of footage,

219
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:03,420
the Thai Navy eventually handed over after two years of negotiation,

220
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:07,800
went on to win a BAFTA nomination and a string of Critics' Choice Awards.

221
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:09,780
It was still snubbed at the Oscars.

222
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:14,040
Chapter nine, still diving eight years later.

223
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:20,140
May 2019, 2026. Eight villagers panning for gold enter

224
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:22,220
a flooded mine in Zaysenbound Province,

225
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:24,480
Laos. Monsoon rain traps,

226
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,520
seven of them underground.

227
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:28,780
Roughly 100 rescuers respond.

228
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,400
Specialists from Thailand,

229
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:33,060
Finland, France, Indonesia,

230
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:35,660
Malaysia, Japan, and Australia.

231
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:40,480
Two of the divers who answer the call are Mikko Parsi and Norris F.

232
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:43,980
Palassri, the same men who dove into Tamloang in 2018.

233
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,520
This time, it isn't a clean ending.

234
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:50,900
Five survivors are found alive by May 30th.

235
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:52,620
Two miners are never located.

236
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:56,280
A cave -in and a real earthquake make the site too unstable.

237
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:59,240
And on June 6th, officials call off the search.

238
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:05,320
One miner is pulled out in a high -risk underwater evacuation on May 29th.

239
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:07,800
The last four walk out on their own the next day,

240
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,880
once the water finally drops low enough.

241
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:16,100
A few weeks later, Chang Rai holds its eighth anniversary memorial for the Tamloang rescue,

242
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:17,900
a tribute to Saman Kunan,

